WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.847 --> 00:00:03.668
In the workshop of the plant lies a block of steel.

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.523
The plate for the filling unit of line 3 comes from it.

3
00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:11.322
The drawing asks for a plate with four holes.

4
00:00:12.025 --> 00:00:15.148
The product runs through them into the cartons on the belt.

5
00:00:16.205 --> 00:00:20.652
Machining means making a part by cutting away material in small curls,

6
00:00:20.825 --> 00:00:23.194
until the shape on the drawing is left.

7
00:00:24.225 --> 00:00:27.336
Six topics follow the plate, from block to measurement.

8
00:00:28.103 --> 00:00:31.180
Turning, milling and drilling are the three ways of cutting.

9
00:00:32.267 --> 00:00:34.601
You need the other three at every cut.

10
00:00:35.391 --> 00:00:38.874
They are the program, the tool and the workholding with measuring.

11
00:00:40.229 --> 00:00:41.692
The first topic is Turning.

12
00:00:42.392 --> 00:00:46.212
The pipe of the tank meets the back of the plate with a round connector.

13
00:00:46.927 --> 00:00:48.320
You make that on a lathe.

14
00:00:49.335 --> 00:00:52.806
The workpiece turns and a stationary tool moves along it.

15
00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.111
That makes round shapes.

16
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.886
For turning we often use a carbide insert.

17
00:01:00.246 --> 00:01:01.860
The second topic is Milling.

18
00:01:02.597 --> 00:01:06.115
Now the tool turns and the workpiece is held on the table.

19
00:01:07.094 --> 00:01:11.344
First you make the top flat, so the plate sits snug against the frame.

20
00:01:12.066 --> 00:01:13.982
Then the tool follows the outline.

21
00:01:14.973 --> 00:01:18.270
For milling we often use a face mill and an end mill.

22
00:01:19.556 --> 00:01:20.996
The third topic is Drilling.

23
00:01:21.704 --> 00:01:26.267
A rotating drill makes the four holes, usually on the same milling machine.

24
00:01:27.291 --> 00:01:32.341
Every hole has to be in its place, so the product falls exactly into a carton.

25
00:01:33.445 --> 00:01:37.009
For drilling we often use a centre drill and a twist drill.

26
00:01:38.303 --> 00:01:40.590
The fourth topic is CNC programming.

27
00:01:41.309 --> 00:01:44.932
A computer drives the motors of the machine, following a program.

28
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:48.678
Every line of the program is one move of the tool.

29
00:01:49.346 --> 00:01:51.447
So every plate comes out the same.

30
00:01:52.449 --> 00:01:55.584
The machine has to know where the plate lies on the table.

31
00:01:56.263 --> 00:01:58.898
Otherwise the holes end up in the wrong place.

32
00:01:59.905 --> 00:02:03.469
For CNC we often use G-code and a work offset.

33
00:02:04.816 --> 00:02:06.360
The fifth topic is Tooling.

34
00:02:07.099 --> 00:02:11.104
The cutting edge is a hard, sharp edge that peels a chip off the plate.

35
00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:14.440
That edge gets hot and has to stay hard.

36
00:02:15.213 --> 00:02:17.733
And it has to suit the material, here steel.

37
00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:21.033
For tooling we often use a tool holder.

38
00:02:21.769 --> 00:02:24.730
And a sister tool, which hangs ready as a spare.

39
00:02:26.024 --> 00:02:28.613
The sixth topic is Workholding and measuring.

40
00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:33.529
The workholding keeps the plate in exactly the same place every time,

41
00:02:33.703 --> 00:02:35.886
firmly against the cutting forces.

42
00:02:36.964 --> 00:02:39.588
Then you measure whether the plate matches the drawing.

43
00:02:40.303 --> 00:02:43.217
Otherwise the holes do not stand above the cartons.

44
00:02:44.216 --> 00:02:48.523
For workholding and measuring we often use a fixture and a micrometer.

45
00:02:49.557 --> 00:02:51.322
The plate is measured and good.

46
00:02:52.077 --> 00:02:55.351
It goes to hall B, to the filling unit of line 3.

47
00:02:56.665 --> 00:02:57.896
This is the whole map.

48
00:02:58.637 --> 00:03:01.656
Machining is the second station of Making things.

49
00:03:02.687 --> 00:03:04.359
Every topic has four levels.

50
00:03:05.358 --> 00:03:07.622
Start with Turning, at Basics level.

51
00:03:08.326 --> 00:03:11.345
That first lesson shows all the ways of machining.

52
00:03:12.365 --> 00:03:16.754
At Working knowledge level you choose cutting data and make holes to size.

53
00:03:17.471 --> 00:03:20.745
You read a program, follow the wear and measure the part.

54
00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:25.865
At Advanced level come finishing, milling strategy and deep holes.

55
00:03:26.654 --> 00:03:29.905
Then offsets, tool life and measurement uncertainty.

56
00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:34.864
At Expert level you work in one setup and guard the hole position.

57
00:03:35.586 --> 00:03:40.080
You use CAM, work out the cost per part and make the process capable.

58
00:03:41.083 --> 00:03:45.135
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
